{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>At the end of three years.</b> If one did not separate the tithes of the first year and the second before their cancellation (shemitah), Scripture obligates him to clear them from the house in the third year, and he must bring to Jerusalem the tithe of the first year that is in his possession, and make the declaration of ״בערתי הקדש מן הבית״ — 'I have cleared the consecrated portion from the house.' Then the Levite comes and takes the first tithe, and the stranger, the orphan, and the widow take the poor man's tithe; and it is not eaten in Jerusalem in the manner you did with the second tithe of the two years."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:19.226730620Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}